The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
root = create_xe_sriov_kobj(xe, PFID); // returns kobj without initializing
err = devm_add_action_or_reset(xe->drm.dev, action_put_kobject, root);
err = kobject_init_and_add(root, &xe_sriov_dev_ktype, parent, "sriov_admin");
```
and:
```
kobj = create_xe_sriov_kobj(xe, VFID(n)); // similar issue
err = devm_add_action_or_reset(xe->drm.dev, action_put_kobject, root); // wrong: should be kobj
```
Reason:
`devm_add_action_or_reset()` will run the cleanup action (`kobject_put`) immediately if it fails, but at that point the kobject is not yet initialized (no `kobject_init` or `kobject_init_and_add` has been called). This causes warnings about uninitialized kobject and refcount underflow. Additionally, in `pf_setup_tree`, the cleanup action is registered on the parent `root` instead of the newly created `kobj`, leading to leaks of the child kobjects.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
// In create_xe_sriov_kobj:
kobject_init(&vkobj->base, ktype);
err = devm_add_action_or_reset(xe->drm.dev, action_put_kobject, &vkobj->base);
if (err) return ERR_PTR(err);
```
and:
```
// In pf_setup_root:
root = create_xe_sriov_kobj(xe, PFID, &xe_sriov_dev_ktype);
if (IS_ERR(root)) return pf_sysfs_error(xe, PTR_ERR(root), "root obj");
err = kobject_add(root, parent, "sriov_admin");
```
and:
```
// In pf_setup_tree:
kobj = create_xe_sriov_kobj(xe, VFID(n), &xe_sriov_vf_ktype);
if (IS_ERR(kobj)) return pf_sysfs_error(xe, PTR_ERR(kobj), "tree obj");
err = kobject_add(kobj, root, ...);
```
Reason:
Now the kobject is properly initialized with `kobject_init()` before the cleanup action is registered via `devm_add_action_or_reset()`. If the registration fails, the cleanup action (`kobject_put`) is called on an initialized kobject, avoiding the warnings. `kobject_add()` is called separately after the cleanup action is safely set up. Also, the cleanup action now correctly references the new kobject (not the parent), preventing leaks and ensuring proper lifetime management for each child kobject.

